{"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "chunk_id": "ASM-07:rec:ASM-037", "content_sha256": "4578651d23b03866aba233c18ba567d342d51611531f7d4e0c42fc803be49b1d", "heading": "ASM-037", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-037", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-037", "text": "### ASM-037 — Shared stimulus boxes feed concept-switching parts\n\n**Claim:** a single stimulus box can feed a run of parts that each interrogate a\ndifferent concept of the same list.\n**Evidence:** the 2CR opening question gives \"The box gives the names of some gases\nin the atmosphere. argon carbon dioxide helium nitrogen oxygen\" with the rule \"Each\ngas may be used once, more than once or not at all.\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/questions.md lines 9-23), then asks identification parts across\nnoble gases, compounds, abundance and greenhouse chemistry (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/questions.md lines 20-34).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "chunk_id": "ASM-07:rec:ASM-038", "content_sha256": "714d691ce218ccd7cd8205057a2005d419fde83bf0e1a159b1baa04cc258c8be", "heading": "ASM-038", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-038", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-038", "text": "### ASM-038 — Consequential marking chains answers across parts\n\n**Claim:** mark schemes explicitly chain later parts onto earlier answers (CSQ), so\nthe papers build multi-step dependencies inside one question.\n**Evidence:** the precipitate-identity part is marked \"silver bromide / LiBr Mark CSQ\non (a) and (b)\" in its guidance — the parsed line reads \"silver bromide / LiBr Mark\nCSQ on (a) and\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 204-218); the\n2C concentration calculation carries \"Mark CSQ on (b)(ii)\" .\n**Design reading:** CSQ is candidate-friendly — a wrong early answer can still earn\nlater method marks — and revision should rehearse recovery, not restart.\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "chunk_id": "ASM-07:rec:ASM-039", "content_sha256": "836b74484ba91be6271305043b504f8cb378fef4e5e828b956290bd08255ab25", "heading": "ASM-039", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-039", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-039", "text": "### ASM-039 — Investigation chains weave technique, observation and explanation\n\n**Claim:** extended investigations integrate apparatus, data handling and explanation\ninto one tariffed chain.\n**Evidence:** the chromatography investigation runs from setup (the parsed excerpt) through\ncolour-counting to solubility explanation across its parts .\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "chunk_id": "ASM-07:rec:ASM-040", "content_sha256": "5e3d2363b12ea4a469f0d9f969301745f994cb1c56c26d3cf180911878b5f79e", "heading": "ASM-040", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-040", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-040", "text": "### ASM-040 — One question, several specification strands\n\n**Claim:** single questions can span distinct specification strands — the flame-test\nquestion combines flame chemistry, precipitation testing and metal-property\nreasoning.\n**Evidence:** the ion-formula part (the parsed excerpt is followed\nby precipitate naming \nand a metal-properties table task (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 221-235).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "chunk_id": "ASM-07:rec:ASM-041", "content_sha256": "e78fe837aa9b7e6b735c7d44bbac5601f6cf201788380861a7f054c85a036cfa", "heading": "ASM-041", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-041", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-041", "text": "### ASM-041 — Concept ladders inside a part-set\n\n**Claim:** part-sets climb a concept ladder — from naming a member of a class to\nclassifying by structure to explaining by properties.\n**Evidence:** the gases run moves from \"Identify the two noble gases\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/questions.md lines 9-23) through compound and abundance\nidentification (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/questions.md lines 20-34) to the\ngreenhouse classification (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/questions.md lines 46-60), and the wire-cleaning part adds the practical-hygiene concept (\"State why the wire should be clean when used in the flame test\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-1C/questions.md lines 204-218)\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "chunk_id": "ASM-07:rec:ASM-042", "content_sha256": "d127e4f50846101eb9e90deac1280d07b2a2d137740a98dff96d95aaaeea50e5", "heading": "ASM-042", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "ASM-07", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-005", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "f61a5bafe6cacdf538e5e06d86f818e7737cbfe3", "syllabai_resources": "367b5d61cd5f1ab115f9947ba2981f08389540ee"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "ASM-042", "research_family": "assessment_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": true, "textbook": false}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "ASM-042", "text": "### ASM-042 — Industrial-process contexts as integration frames\n\n**Claim:** processing contexts (crude-oil separation) frame questions that integrate\nnaming, property and use.\n**Evidence:** the crude-oil question opens \"The diagram shows crude oil being\nseparated into different fractions\" with \"Name the process used to separate crude\noil into different fractions.\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2019-06/4CH1-2CR/questions.md lines 130-144).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
